 ["get_event_detail"]}, {"ref": "E184", "source": "event", "document_name": null, "page_start": null, "cited": true, "retrieved_by": ["get_event_detail"]}, {"ref": "E185", "source": "event", "document_name": null, "page_start": null, "cited": true, "retrieved_by": ["timeline_skeleton"]}, {"ref": "E187", "source": "event", "document_name": null, "page_start": null, "cited": true, "retrieved_by": ["get_event_detail"]}, {"ref": "E189", "source": "event", "document_name": null, "page_start": null, "cited": true, "retrieved_by": ["get_event_detail"]}], "gaps": [], "lint": [], "retrieval": {"rerank": true, "dense": true, "chunks": 353}, "answer": "**Yes — and it is unresolved.** Two grievances, both about the kickoff call.\n\n**1. He believes the sales rep misled him about timing.** In live chat on 2026-09-08 he said Leandro told him the kickoff call happens \"usually within 4 days,\" not a month out, and that a ticket had been opened to move it to 9/9. When support told him no earlier attorney availability exists, he replied: \"I understand that the attorney is busy, but I don't like being lied to\" [E181]. He was explicit that he holds the chat agent blameless, so the friction is with the sales/scheduling promise, not support.\n\n**2. He was planning his life around a date that never got confirmed.** He asked for confirmation of a 9/9 11:00 slot [E176], chased it by SMS — \"I cannot verify it by myself. Please, let me know because I am planning my other appointments around this one\" [E179] — and reported at 16:05 on 2026-09-08 that there was still no confirmation and he still saw 10/2 in the portal [E187].\n\n**Current posture — this is the part that matters:** the paralegal told him at 16:38 on 2026-09-08 to \"keep an eye out today for an update\" [E189], and the record shows no substantive contact since. The kickoff call remains scheduled for 2026-10-02 (internal meeting, not a court date). The 9/9 date he was reorganising appointments around has now passed with no answer either way.\n\nTwo smaller items from the same thread, not complaints but live concerns:\n- He doubts a 20-minute kickoff slot is enough to explain his situation [E176].\n- He is having trouble locating 2024 tax records because the family was in Italy [E176].\n\nContext on satisfaction: he rated the case start 5/5 on 2026-09-05 [E100], so the dissatisfaction is recent and specific to scheduling. Support ticket 01208613 from the chat was marked Solved on 2026-09-08 [E185], and the closing email says \"we were able to help you with your request\" [E184] — that does not match the client's last message, which says nothing was confirmed [E187]."}
